<title>ETHIOPIA: Airline thinks hijackers came from Bombay.</title>
<headline>Airline thinks hijackers came from Bombay.</headline>
<dateline>ADDIS ABABA 1996-11-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The hijackers of an Ethiopian Airlines plane that crashed off the Comoro Islands on Saturday were believed to be transit passengers from Bombay, officials of the airline said.</p>
<p>They said the identity of the hijackers was not confirmed but they may have arrived in Addis Ababa from Bombay and then boarded the Boeing 767 with the goal of hijacking it to Australia, said the officials.</p>
</text>
